  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohit Kumar vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of ... on 21 November, 2024 Author: Alok Mathur Bench: Alok Mathur High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ? Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:77118 Court No. - 6 Case :- Writ - A No. - 10805 of 2024 Petitioner :- Mohit Kumar Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of Food And Civil Supply Lko And An Counsel for Petitioner :- Abhishek Tiwari,Anuj Kudesia,Rishabh Chauhan Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Alok Mathur,J. 1.",
    "facts": "The preliminary inquiry was got conducted by a team consisting with Supply Inspector, Marketing Inspector, Food Safety Officials, who found that between 40 to 60 bags of wheat food-grains which was not fit for human consumption had been dispatched to various fair price shops for distribution. In the preliminary inquiry report the role of the petitioner was also highlighted and it is for the said reason that District Magistrate, Shahjahanpur after considering the preliminary inquiry report had issued a direction on 15.10.2024 to take action against all the persons responsible and to suspend them and also to initiate disciplinary proceedings. It is in pursuance of the order of the District Magistrate that the petitioner by means of the impugned order dated 19.10.2024 has been suspended.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner has vehemently submitted that the petitioner is not involved at any stage and the allegations of the preliminary report does not record any finding involving petitioner and also that the order for holding inquiry in the said matter has been passed without any application of mind."
  },
